    "shadow": "The same instinct fires early at work, and a door gets closed that only needed adjusting. A clumsy email, a client who oversteps once, a manager who misreads a decision, and your resignation is already written in your head by lunchtime. You leave roles at the first structural insult and carry the story of principle out with you, while the record collects short tenures that nobody quite understands. Underneath runs a fear of being discarded or exposed as unnecessary, so you exit first, before anyone else is given the chance to move you. What it costs is the long arc: the reform that only lands for the people who stayed through three difficult quarters.",
