    "shadow": "Agitation makes stable work feel unbearable, and stability is exactly what most jobs eventually offer. A quarter runs smoothly, a role settles into competence, and you start manufacturing friction: a reorganisation nobody asked for, a confrontation staged in a meeting, a departure floated to see who reacts to it. Colleagues learn to brace whenever your energy goes restless, and your reputation splits between brilliant and unsafe to build anything around. Underneath runs a suspicion that you only matter mid-crisis, that a thing being maintained has no further use for you. The cost is the compounding work you never see through, the second and third year where what you began would finally have counted.",
